  "worked_solution": "We multiply each entry of $F$ by $4$ and each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{2},$ and then subtract the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4F-\\frac{1}{2}G & =4[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 0 & 2\\end{aligned}]-\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 & 4 & -6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4\\cdot 4 & 4\\cdot (-1) & 4\\cdot 0 & 4\\cdot 2\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4 & \\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16 & -4 & 0 & 8\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}16-1 & -4-0 & 0-2 & 8-(-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}15 & -4 & -2 & 11\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
